From 586cae395da8a2cacfb12adea0cf3994867fbcfb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 11:13:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] gateway: take launchd ExitTimeOut from the launcher
 when sandboxed (gateway-64b702b67e)

The mini's com.daveey.myapp.hermes-household / -standard gateways run as
`hermes-gateway-launcher -- /usr/bin/sandbox-exec -p <profile> hermes gateway run`, and the profile
denies process-exec of /bin/launchctl (deliberate escape guard). read_launchd_exit_timeout_s's
`launchctl print` therefore always failed there, _assumed_launchd_exit_timeout assumed the 60s gui
clamp and wrote a launchd_budget_missing row, while launchd SIGKILLs these jobs at 45s, so a
signal-driven drain could outrun the SIGKILL by 15s.

The unsandboxed launcher (state e84f55624) now probes once and exports HERMES_LAUNCHD_EXIT_TIMEOUT_S.
read_launchd_exit_timeout_s uses it (positive integer, else ignored) only when its own probe fails or
finds no `exit timeout` line and a job label is known; a working live probe still wins. The boot log
says "(from launcher)", and no launchd_budget_missing row is written in that case.

Proof: tests/gateway/test_launchd_exit_timeout_from_launcher.py red 4 failed / 11 passed before
(probe raises/nonzero + env 45 -> None; boot loader assumed 60 and logged launchd_budget_missing),
15 passed after; with test_launchd_explicit_label, test_launchd_exit_timeout_drain_cap and
test_launchd_label_reaches_gateway: 40 passed.
Card: t_01a1c51ebad6c41c
